['Engineers India Limited (EIL) has been the front-runner in delivering services to various clients for green hydrogen projects that are critical to the decarbonization of multiple industries. A notable project in this regard is a 10 MW Green Hydrogen plant in Vijaipur that uses state-of-the-art Proton Exchange Membrane (PEM) technology. The unit, designed to produce 4.3 tonnes per day (TPD) of green hydrogen using renewable energy from the grid, was successfully commissioned recently. EIL is also capable of blending green hydrogen in natural gas pipelines and city gas distribution networks.

@hardeepspuri @sureshgopi 
